<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaius Hostilius Mancinus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2nd century BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaius Hostilius Mancinus was a Roman consul of 137 BCE who commanded against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/numantia">Numantia</a> in the Numantine War. Trapped by the Numantines, he surrendered with about 20,000 men and accepted a treaty negotiated by his quaestor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a> Sempronius Gracchus. The Senate repudiated the treaty and handed Mancinus over, bound, to the Numantines, who refused to accept him.</p></div>
